+
+# --batch, with an engine run with STRATA_READ_YIELD=1 (INFO read_yield=1): a prompt read in progress gives way (BYIELD,
+# #656) to a waiting request that has at most STRATA_YIELD_SHORT new tokens to read (opt-in; unset or 0: the #656 rule as
+# before - a waiting prompt under half the running one's length).  New tokens: the prompt minus the longest start of it a
+# slot holds (slot_held), so a short follow-up in a long conversation counts as short (the engine's RAM cache is not
+# seen here: the estimate errs towards not yielding).  Only while the read has STRATA_YIELD_MIN_LEFT tokens left
+# (default 4 x STRATA_YIELD_SHORT, at least 1024), at most STRATA_YIELDS_MAX times per request (default 2), asked again
+# STRATA_YIELD_RETRY_S after the engine answered YIELDNO (default 2).  A read that may give way takes a slot the engine can
+# keep it in (INFO yield_row=k: b % k == k - 1, the top row of a pipelined group), the one that widens its group least
+# (STRATA_YIELD_TOP_ROW=0: the usual slot choice, and such a read does not give way unless it lands there).
+YIELD_SHORT = max(0, _int_env("STRATA_YIELD_SHORT", 0))
